            "text": "Adaptive financial crime and high-velocity fraud represent key challenges in digital banking. Fraud patterns evolve over time, necessitating continuous learning in detection models to counter adversarial adaptation (e.g., fraudsters modifying tactics to bypass detection). However, the paper does not specify detailed fraud operation tactics (e.g., phishing, identity theft, synthetic account creation) or provide indicator-of-compromise (IoC) data.",
